{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"language":"python","display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.11.11","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":11494122,"datasetId":7205353,"databundleVersionId":11941260}],"dockerImageVersionId":31012,"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"<h1>🌍 VirtuTrek : AI-Powered Virtual Tour Assistant</h1>\n\n<h3>📌 Problem Statement</h3>\n\nMillions of people want to explore the world’s most beautiful heritage sites — from the Great Zimbabwe Walls to the Pyramids of Egypt — but many face barriers like distance, limited information, or lack of personal guides. Traditional travel apps offer generic content, and heritage education often lacks engagement.\n\n<h3>🧠 Why Generative AI?</h3>\nGenerative AI provides an opportunity to transform how we experience culture and travel. With tools like Gemini, LangChain, and RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation), we can:\n\n* Analyze images of heritage sites in real-time\n\n* Understand the user’s mood and preferences\n\n* Generate detailed and human-like travel itineraries\n\n* Offer conversational guidance using intelligent sub-agents\n\n* Translate and adapt tours in multiple languages\n\n* Narrate tours like a human guide — in text and audio\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n<h3>🧭 What is VirtuTrek?</h3>\nVirtuTrek is a personalized AI travel assistant that turns any photo into an interactive experience. Whether you're uploading a landmark image, chatting with a smart agent, or planning a custom tour — the system adapts to your needs using cutting-edge GenAI technologies.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"<h1>🧩 System Overview</h1>\n\nVirtuTrek is composed of three smart modules working together:\n\n<h5>1️⃣ 🖼 Image-to-Insight (Image Analysis Module)</h5>\n* Upload an image of any landmark, and Gemini identifies the location, provides detailed historical descriptions, and maps the location.\n\n* The system also narrates the result using text-to-speech (TTS) and suggests a travel route using OpenRouteService.\n\n* Bonus: Real-time weather info is fetched using OpenWeatherMap API.\n\n  \n\n<h5>2️⃣ 💬 AI Tour Guide (Chatbot Module)</h5>\n\n* A multi-agent system powered by LangChain and Gemini.\n\n* Automatically detects the topic of your question (architecture, logistics, history, etc.) and routes it to a specialized sub-agent.\n\n* Engages in friendly, personalized conversations just like a human tour guide.\n\n  \n\n<h5>3️⃣ 🗺 Personalized Tour Planner (RAG Module)</h5>\n\n* Collects user preferences (mood, interests, city).\n\n* Fetches content from Wikipedia and processes it using Sentence Transformers.\n\n* Stores embeddings in FAISS, retrieves relevant chunks, and generates custom tour plans using Gemini.\n\n  \n\n<h5>🧠 How It Works</h5>\n\nEach module functions independently, but all are unified through a Streamlit dashboard for seamless navigation. Users can explore the system by selecting services from a sidebar, allowing them to switch between visual exploration, personalized itinerary planning, and conversational assistance.\n\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"For more Explanation and Demo, visit out <a href = \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hSdERVNZOrc\">YouTube</a> and our <a href = \"https://medium.com/@anandumallya/virtutrek-our-ai-travel-companion-6c0f5e879f0e\">Blog</a>","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"Have a visit to our deployed app VirtuTrek: <a href = \"https://virtutrek.streamlit.app/\">VirtuTrek-App</a>","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# ✅ Installing all required dependencies","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import os\nimport sys\nimport subprocess\n\ndef install(package):\n    subprocess.check_call([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", package])\n\n# List of (package_import_name, pip_install_name) pairs\npackages = [\n    (\"langchain_google_genai\", \"langchain_google_genai\"),\n    (\"langchain\", \"langchain\"),\n    (\"langchain_community\", \"langchain_community\"),\n    (\"requests\", \"requests\"),\n    (\"dotenv\", \"python-dotenv\"),  # .env handling\n    (\"streamlit\", \"streamlit\"),   # Works but Streamlit apps can't run natively on Kaggle\n    (\"PIL\", \"Pillow\"),\n    (\"googlemaps\", \"googlemaps\"),\n    (\"geopy\", \"geopy\"),\n    (\"google.generativeai\", \"google-generativeai\"),  # Special import\n    (\"pydeck\", \"pydeck\"),\n    (\"gtts\", \"gTTS\"),\n    (\"folium\", \"folium\"),\n    (\"streamlit_folium\", \"streamlit-folium\"),\n    (\"openrouteservice\", \"openrouteservice\"),\n    (\"faiss\", \"faiss-cpu\"),\n    (\"numpy\", \"numpy\"),\n    (\"nltk\", \"nltk\"),\n    (\"sentence_transformers\", \"sentence-transformers\"),\n    (\"serpapi\", \"google-search-results\"),\n]\n\nfor import_name, pip_name in packages:\n    try:\n        __import__(import_name)\n        print(f\"✅ {pip_name} is already installed.\")\n    except ImportError:\n        print(f\"⬇️ Installing {pip_name}...\")\n        install(pip_name)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-04-21T03:51:07.609305Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-04-21T03:51:07.609619Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-04-21T03:51:08.619376Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-04-21T03:51:07.609589Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-04-21T03:51:08.618528Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"!pip install nest_asyncio","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-04-21T03:21:42.241375Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-04-21T03:21:42.242152Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-04-21T03:21:45.886613Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-04-21T03:21:42.242128Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-04-21T03:21:45.885707Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Additional Imports","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from langchain_community.utilities import SerpAPIWrapper\nimport requests\nfrom langchain.tools import Tool\nfrom langchain_google_genai import ChatGoogleGenerativeAI\nfrom langchain.agents import initialize_agent, AgentType\nimport asyncio\nimport re\nimport nest_asyncio\nnest_asyncio.apply()  # Allows nested event loops in Jupyter/Kaggle :contentReference[oaicite:9]{index=9}\n","metadata":{"_uuid":"8f2839f25d086af736a60e9eeb907d3b93b6e0e5","_cell_guid":"b1076dfc-b9ad-4769-8c92-a6c4dae69d19","trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-04-21T03:21:45.887714Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-04-21T03:21:45.887997Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-04-21T03:21:47.781676Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-04-21T03:21:45.887957Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-04-21T03:21:47.780794Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### Setting up APIs","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from kaggle_secrets import UserSecretsClient\nuser_secrets = UserSecretsClient()\ngoogle_api_key = user_secrets.get_secret(\"GOOGLE_API_KEY\")\ngooglemaps_api_key = user_secrets.get_secret(\"GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY\")\nopenroute_api_key = user_secrets.get_secret(\"OPENROUTESERVICE_API_KEY\")\nserpapi_api_key = user_secrets.get_secret(\"SERPAPI_API_KEY\")\nweather_api_key = user_secrets.get_secret(\"WEATHER_API_KEY\")\nopenweather_api_key = user_secrets.get_secret(\"OPENWEATHER_API_KEY\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-04-21T03:21:47.789245Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-04-21T03:21:47.789573Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-04-21T03:21:49.292487Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-04-21T03:21:47.789544Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-04-21T03:21:49.291503Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### AI Agent Tools\n\n🔧 Tools for the AI Chatbot Agent\nWe define LangChain-compatible tools to enhance the chatbot’s ability to answer diverse user queries:\n\nWeb Search Tool: Uses SerpAPI to perform live Google searches. This allows the chatbot to answer real-time questions like \"What is the capital of France?\"\n\nWeather Search Tool: Connects to WeatherAPI to fetch current weather data for a given city. Useful for queries like \"How’s the weather in Paris?\"\n\nThese tools are combined into a tools list, enabling the agent to dynamically select and use them during conversation.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"\ndef search_google(query: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Search Google using SerpAPI.\"\"\"\n        serp = SerpAPIWrapper(serpapi_api_key= serpapi_api_key)\n        results = serp.run(query)\n        return results","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-04-21T03:21:49.293468Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-04-21T03:21:49.293745Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-04-21T03:21:49.298829Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-04-21T03:21:49.293723Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-04-21T03:21:49.298005Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"def get_weather(city:str):\n        params = {\n            \"q\": city,\n            \"key\": weather_api_key,\n            \"aqi\": \"yes\"\n        }\n        response = requests.get(\"https://api.weatherapi.com/v1/current.json\", params=params).json()\n\n        #print(json.dumps(response, indent=2))  # Debug the full response\n\n        if \"current\" in response:\n            return f\"\"\"Weather in {city}:\n                    - Condition: {response[\"current\"][\"condition\"][\"text\"]}\n                    - Temperature: {response[\"current\"][\"temp_c\"]}°C\n                    - Feels Like: {response[\"current\"][\"feelslike_c\"]}°C\n                    - Humidity: {response[\"current\"][\"humidity\"]}%\n                    - Wind Speed: {response[\"current\"][\"wind_kph\"]} kph\n                    - UV Index: {response[\"current\"].get(\"uv\", \"N/A\")}\n                    \"\"\"\n        return \"Weather data not available.\"","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-04-21T03:21:53.16374Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-04-21T03:21:53.164114Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-04-21T03:21:53.170224Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-04-21T03:21:53.164087Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-04-21T03:21:53.169056Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"web_search = Tool(\n        name = \"Web Search\",\n        func=search_google,\n        description=\"A tool to search the web using Google. Input should be a string like 'What is the capital of France?'.\",\n    )\n\ngetweather = Tool(\n    name = \"Weather Search\",\n    func=get_weather,\n    description=\"A tool to get teh weather o fteh heritage site or any city. Input should be a string like 'how is the weather in Paris?'.\",\n)\n\ntools = [web_search, getweather]","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-04-21T03:22:01.138532Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-04-21T03:22:01.138855Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-04-21T03:22:01.144052Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-04-21T03:22:01.138827Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-04-21T03:22:01.143241Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Chatbot\n\nThe chatbot in VirtuTrek functions as a virtual tour guide, enabling users to ask questions about heritage sites, history, architecture, weather, and travel logistics. It intelligently categorizes user queries using a categorizer agent and delegates responses to specialized GenAI-powered sub-agents like historical expert, weather forecaster, and conversational guide. The chatbot uses LangChain's agent framework with Google Gemini (via ChatGoogleGenerativeAI) to generate accurate, context-aware responses. It also integrates SerpAPI and WeatherAPI tools to fetch real-time data when needed. This multi-agent architecture ensures rich, dynamic, and personalized user interaction.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### Categorizer Agent: \nClassifies user queries into categories like history, architecture, travel, dining, and more using Gemini.\n\n#### History Expert Subagent: \nProvides historical facts, timelines, and stories about heritage sites using Gemini's structured reasoning.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"class CategorizerAgent:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.llm = ChatGoogleGenerativeAI(model=\"gemini-2.0-flash\", google_api_key = google_api_key)\n        self.tools = tools\n        self.agent = initialize_agent(\n            tools=self.tools,\n            llm=self.llm,\n            agent=AgentType.ZERO_SHOT_REACT_DESCRIPTION,\n            verbose=True,\n            handle_parsing_errors=True\n        )\n    \n    async def categorize_topic(self, text,timeout=30):\n        prompt = f\"\"\"\n        You are the Categorizer Agent, a specialized AI component responsible for analyzing the user's input {text} and classifying it into one of the predefined categories based strictly on the content and intent of the message.\n\n        Your job is to accurately detect the user’s intent and return only the matching category label from the list below. You should not perform any processing or delegation yourself — your role is limited to categorization only.\n\n        📋 Available Categories\n        Choose only one of the following:\n\n        \"Historical Information\" – if the user is asking about the history of a place, monument, or heritage site.\n\n        \"Architectural Details\" – if the user is interested in design, structure, style, or architecture of a place.\n\n        \"Travel or Logistics\" – if the user is asking about how to reach a place, travel duration, entry fee, timings, routes, etc.\n\n        \"Accommodation and Dining\" – if the user is seeking places to stay, eat, nearby attractions, or leisure activities.\n\n        \"General Conversation\" – if the user is making casual remarks, greetings, jokes, or off-topic chit-chat.\n        \n        \"Weather Information\"  if the user is asking about the weather of a place.\n\n        \"Unrecognized\" – if the input does not fit into any of the above categories.\n\n        ✅ Output Format\n        Return only a single line of text with just the category label, nothing else.\n        Do not explain or comment on your decision. Do not repeat the input.\n        \"\"\"\n        response = await self.llm.ainvoke(prompt)\n        # If 'response' is an AIMessage object, extract its content first\n        response = response.content if hasattr(response, 'content') else response\n        \n        # Clean markdown-style formatting (if any)\n        response = re.sub(r\"^```json|```$\", \"\", response).strip()\n\n        try:\n            return response\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            return {\"error\": \"Invalid JSON format returned\", \"raw_response\": response}\n\n\nclass History_Expert_Subagent:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.llm = ChatGoogleGenerativeAI(model=\"gemini-2.0-flash\", google_api_key = google_api_key)\n        self.tools = tools\n        self.agent = initialize_agent(\n            tools=self.tools,\n            llm=self.llm,\n            agent=AgentType.ZERO_SHOT_REACT_DESCRIPTION,\n            verbose=True,\n            handle_parsing_errors=True\n        )\n    \n    async def history_info(self, text):\n        prompt = f\"\"\"\n            You are the History Expert Subagent, responsible for providing detailed, accurate, and insightful historical context for any heritage site, landmark, or culturally significant location the user inquires about.\n\n            Your responsibilities:\n\n            Provide verified historical facts (e.g., date of construction, founder, purpose, major events).\n\n            Highlight the cultural and political significance of the location.\n\n            Mention any legends, folklore, or myths associated with the place, if applicable.\n\n            Be clear, concise, and structured — no fluff or filler.\n            \n            user input: {text}\n\n            Return your output in this format:\n\n            Name of Site:\n            Historical Overview:\n            Timeline of Key Events:\n            Interesting Facts or Stories:\n            Source Reliability: High / Medium / Low\n        \"\"\"\n        response = await self.llm.ainvoke(prompt)\n        response = response.content if hasattr(response, 'content') else response\n        \n        # Clean markdown-style formatting (if any)\n        response = re.sub(r\"^```json|```$\", \"\", response).strip()\n\n        try:\n            return response\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            return {\"error\": \"Invalid JSON format returned\", \"raw_response\": response}","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-04-21T03:22:31.430494Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-04-21T03:22:31.43118Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-04-21T03:22:31.441611Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-04-21T03:22:31.431148Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-04-21T03:22:31.440578Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### Weather Forecaster Subagent: \nExtracts the user’s intended location, fetches live weather data, and summarizes it in a friendly format using Gemini.\n\n#### Architectural Expert Subagent: \nUses Gemini to describe the style, materials, and artistic features of landmarks in a structured and insightful way.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"class Weather_forecaster_Subagent:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.llm = ChatGoogleGenerativeAI(model=\"gemini-2.0-flash\", google_api_key = google_api_key)\n        self.tools = tools\n        self.agent = initialize_agent(\n            tools=self.tools,\n            llm=self.llm,\n            agent=AgentType.ZERO_SHOT_REACT_DESCRIPTION,\n            verbose=True,\n            handle_parsing_errors=True\n        )\n    \n    async def weather_info(self, text):\n        prompt = f\"\"\"\n                    You are a Weather Location Extractor Subagent. Your job is to extract the name of the city or place the user is asking about in their query.\n\n                    Only return the name of the city or place — nothing else.\n\n                    The place name should be suitable to pass into a weather API.\n\n                    User input: {text}\n\n                    Extracted location:\n                \"\"\"\n\n        response = await self.llm.ainvoke(prompt)\n        response = response.content if hasattr(response, 'content') else response\n        \n        # Clean markdown-style formatting (if any)\n        response = re.sub(r\"^```json|```$\", \"\", response).strip()\n\n        try:\n            result = get_weather(response)\n            prompt = f\"you are a weather forecaster, you are ordered to provide weatehr details ina systematic and easy way fro teh user to understand by using the providee weather details: {result}\"\n            response = self.llm.invoke(prompt).content.strip()\n            return response\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            return {\"error\": \"Invalid JSON format returned\", \"raw_response\": response}\n\n\nclass Architectural_Expert_Subagent:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.llm = ChatGoogleGenerativeAI(model=\"gemini-2.0-flash\", google_api_key = google_api_key)\n        self.tools = tools\n        self.agent = initialize_agent(\n            tools=self.tools,\n            llm=self.llm,\n            agent=AgentType.ZERO_SHOT_REACT_DESCRIPTION,\n            verbose=True,\n            handle_parsing_errors=True\n        )\n    \n    async def architecture_info(self, text):\n        prompt = f\"\"\"\n        You are the Architectural Expert Subagent, responsible for analyzing and explaining the structural, stylistic, and artistic aspects of a monument, temple, fort, or other built heritage.\n\n        Your responsibilities:\n\n        Identify the architectural style (e.g., Mughal, Dravidian, Gothic, Colonial).\n\n        Mention the materials, structural techniques, and artistic features used.\n\n        Point out any symbolic design elements or layout significance.\n\n        Provide comparisons with similar structures if relevant.\n        \n        user input: {text}\n\n        Return your output in this format:\n\n        Name of Site:\n        Architectural Style:\n        Materials Used:\n        Structural Highlights:\n        Artistic Elements (e.g., carvings, frescoes, motifs):\n        Special Features / Innovations:\n        \"\"\"\n        response = await self.llm.ainvoke(prompt)\n        response = response.content if hasattr(response, 'content') else response\n        \n        # Clean markdown-style formatting (if any)\n        response = re.sub(r\"^```json|```$\", \"\", response).strip()\n\n        try:\n            return response\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            return {\"error\": \"Invalid JSON format returned\", \"raw_response\": response}","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-04-21T03:22:53.048747Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-04-21T03:22:53.049107Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-04-21T03:22:53.05992Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-04-21T03:22:53.049081Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-04-21T03:22:53.059024Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### Travel Logistics Subagent: \nUses Gemini to offer transport options, travel time, costs, and accessibility details for reaching heritage sites.\n\n#### Accommodation & Dining Expert Subagent: \nSuggests hotels, food spots, and nearby attractions with cultural tips using Gemini for a tailored travel experience.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"class Travel_Logistics_Subagent:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.llm = ChatGoogleGenerativeAI(model=\"gemini-2.0-flash\", google_api_key = google_api_key)\n        self.tools = tools\n        self.agent = initialize_agent(\n            tools=self.tools,\n            llm=self.llm,\n            agent=AgentType.ZERO_SHOT_REACT_DESCRIPTION,\n            verbose=True,\n            handle_parsing_errors=True\n        )\n    \n    async def travel_info(self, text):\n        prompt = f\"\"\"\n        You are the Travel Logistics Subagent, tasked with providing up-to-date and practical information on how to reach a specific tourist location.\n\n        Your responsibilities:\n\n        Provide recommended modes of transport (train, bus, flight, taxi).\n\n        Mention nearest transport hubs (airport, railway station).\n\n        Approximate travel time and cost from common points (e.g., major cities).\n\n        Include entry fees, opening/closing times, and best visiting seasons.\n\n        Mention accessibility (elderly-friendly, wheelchair access, etc.) if applicable.\n        \n        user input: {text}\n\n        Return your output in this format:\n\n        Location:\n        Nearest Airport/Station:\n        Travel Options:\n        Travel Duration & Cost Estimates:\n        Entry Fee & Timings:\n        Best Time to Visit:\n        Accessibility Notes:\n\n        \"\"\"\n        response = await self.llm.ainvoke(prompt)\n        response = response.content if hasattr(response, 'content') else response\n        \n        # Clean markdown-style formatting (if any)\n        response = re.sub(r\"^```json|```$\", \"\", response).strip()\n\n        try:\n            return response\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            return {\"error\": \"Invalid JSON format returned\", \"raw_response\": response}\n\n\nclass Accommodation_and_Dining_Expert_Subagent:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.llm = ChatGoogleGenerativeAI(model=\"gemini-2.0-flash\", google_api_key = google_api_key)\n        self.tools = tools\n        self.agent = initialize_agent(\n            tools=self.tools,\n            llm=self.llm,\n            agent=AgentType.ZERO_SHOT_REACT_DESCRIPTION,\n            verbose=True,\n            handle_parsing_errors=True\n        )\n    \n    async def accommodation_info(self, text):\n        prompt = f\"\"\"\n        You are the Accommodation and Dining Expert Subagent, responsible for suggesting where to stay, what to eat, and what else to explore nearby.\n\n        Your responsibilities:\n\n        Recommend accommodations across budget ranges (luxury, mid-range, budget).\n\n        Suggest authentic or popular local dining spots.\n\n        Recommend nearby attractions and activities for tourists.\n\n        Mention safety tips and local etiquette if relevant.\n        \n        user input: {text}\n\n        Return your output in this format:\n\n        Location:\n        Top Accommodation Picks:\n        - Luxury: \n        - Mid-range: \n        - Budget:\n        Recommended Eateries:\n        - Local Cuisine:\n        - Vegetarian/Vegan Options:\n        Nearby Attractions/Activities:\n        Safety Tips & Local Etiquette:\n        \"\"\"\n        response = await self.llm.ainvoke(prompt)\n        # If 'response' is an AIMessage object, extract its content first\n        response = response.content if hasattr(response, 'content') else response\n        \n        # Clean markdown-style formatting (if any)\n        response = re.sub(r\"^```json|```$\", \"\", response).strip()\n\n        try:\n            return response\n        except json.JSONDecodeError:\n            return {\"error\": \"Invalid JSON format returned\", \"raw_response\": response}","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2025-04-21T03:23:43.233148Z","iopub.execute_input":"2025-04-21T03:23:43.233803Z","iopub.status.idle":"2025-04-21T03:23:43.242795Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2025-04-21T03:23:43.233778Z","shell.execute_reply":"2025-04-21T03:23:43.241778Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### Conversational Tour Guide Subagent: \nMimics a friendly human companion using Gemini to engage users in casual, warm, and context-aware conversations.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"class Conversational_tour_guide_subagent:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.llm = ChatGoogleGenerativeAI(model=\"gemini-2.0-flash\", google_api_key = google_api_key)\n        self.tools = tools\n        self.agent = initialize_agent(\n            tools=self.tools,\n            llm=self.llm,\n            agent=AgentType.ZERO_SHOT_REACT_DESCRIPTION,\n            verbose=True,\n            handle_parsing_errors=True\n        )\n    \n    async def convo_info(self, text):\n        prompt = f\"\"\"\n        You are a Conversational tour guide subagent. Your role is to engage in friendly, casual conversation with users as if you’re accompanying them on a relaxed tour — through a city, a museum, a campus, or even a digital platform.\n\n        Your tone is warm, conversational, and attentive. You don’t wait for commands or tasks; instead, you respond naturally to whatever the user says — like a human guide would during small talk.\n\n        If the user shares a feeling, observation, or random thought, respond with something related, thoughtful, or playful. You are not here to perform tasks, give definitions, or answer deep factual queries — just vibe and keep the energy light, interesting, and human.\n\n        Think of yourself as a mix of a knowledgeable host and a good listener — someone who knows the place well, but never dominates the conversation.\n\n        Keep responses short and context-aware. Ask casual follow-up questions if it feels right. Never prompt the user to “ask a question.” Just go with the flow.\n        \n        user input: {text}\n        \"\"\"\n        response = await self.llm.ainvoke(prompt)\n        # If 'response' is an AIM